1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,438
Pull a suitcase by its handle.

2
00:00:02,438 --> 00:00:04,294
Tow a toy car on a string.

3
00:00:04,294 --> 00:00:06,725
Push a lawn mower by its long handle.

4
00:00:07,125 --> 00:00:11,367
In all three, you pull at a slant,
but the thing moves along the ground.

5
00:00:11,817 --> 00:00:14,203
Aarav drags his suitcase to the bus stop.

6
00:00:14,203 --> 00:00:17,197
He pulls with forty newtons,
along a slanted handle.

7
00:00:17,547 --> 00:00:20,726
How much of his forty newtons
really moves it forward?

8
00:00:20,726 --> 00:00:22,105
All forty, or less?

9
00:00:22,605 --> 00:00:27,081
By the end, you will answer it with
one small tool, the dot product.

10
00:00:27,731 --> 00:00:29,573
So what is the dot product?

11
00:00:29,923 --> 00:00:32,629
Shine a torch straight
down on a slanted stick.

12
00:00:32,629 --> 00:00:35,515
Its shadow on the floor
is shorter than the stick.

13
00:00:35,915 --> 00:00:39,478
That shadow is the part of the
stick that points along the floor.

14
00:00:39,878 --> 00:00:41,861
Now take two arrows, A and B.

15
00:00:41,861 --> 00:00:45,744
Find the shadow of A on B, and
multiply it by the length of B.

16
00:00:46,144 --> 00:00:47,841
That is the dot product.

17
00:00:47,841 --> 00:00:52,339
The answer is just a number, so it
is also called the scalar product.

18
00:00:52,989 --> 00:00:54,746
Let's run it on Aarav's suitcase.

19
00:00:54,746 --> 00:00:57,057
He pulls with a force F of forty newtons.

20
00:00:57,407 --> 00:01:00,479
First, the handle is
flat, so theta is zero.

21
00:01:00,479 --> 00:01:03,763
The shadow of F on the
floor is all forty newtons.

22
00:01:04,163 --> 00:01:06,508
Now he raises the handle to sixty degrees.

23
00:01:06,508 --> 00:01:08,804
The shadow shrinks to just twenty newtons.

24
00:01:09,204 --> 00:01:11,860
The rest of his pull
only lifts the handle.

25
00:01:11,860 --> 00:01:14,181
It does not roll the suitcase forward.

26
00:01:14,581 --> 00:01:17,048
At ninety degrees, he pulls straight up.

27
00:01:17,048 --> 00:01:18,331
The shadow is zero.

28
00:01:18,331 --> 00:01:20,023
The suitcase does not roll.

29
00:01:20,523 --> 00:01:22,495
Slow-mo replay, at sixty degrees.

30
00:01:22,845 --> 00:01:24,696
F points along the handle.

31
00:01:24,696 --> 00:01:27,438
Its shadow on the floor is F cos theta.

32
00:01:27,438 --> 00:01:29,339
The suitcase moves along d.

33
00:01:29,839 --> 00:01:33,650
On the graph, as theta grows,
the forward part falls.

34
00:01:33,650 --> 00:01:35,236
It follows cos theta.

35
00:01:35,886 --> 00:01:38,673
Now the formula, one small step at a time.

36
00:01:39,023 --> 00:01:39,923
Step one.

37
00:01:39,826 --> 00:01:43,714
Theta is the angle between A
and B, measured tail to tail.

38
00:01:44,464 --> 00:01:45,364
Step two.

39
00:01:45,237 --> 00:01:47,732
The shadow of A on B is A cos theta.

40
00:01:47,732 --> 00:01:50,445
Cos theta is the fraction
the shadow keeps.

41
00:01:50,445 --> 00:01:53,986
One at zero degrees, a half
at sixty, zero at ninety.

42
00:01:54,736 --> 00:01:55,636
Step three.

43
00:01:55,618 --> 00:01:57,543
Multiply by the length of B.

44
00:01:57,543 --> 00:01:59,631
A dot B equals AB cos theta.

45
00:02:00,381 --> 00:02:01,281
Step four.

46
00:02:01,214 --> 00:02:04,871
The shadow of B on A, times
A, gives the same number.

47
00:02:04,871 --> 00:02:06,815
So A dot B equals B dot A.

48
00:02:07,565 --> 00:02:08,542
Remember this.

49
00:02:08,542 --> 00:02:11,759
A dot B is one arrow times
the shadow of the other.

50
00:02:11,759 --> 00:02:13,403
A number, not an arrow.

51
00:02:14,103 --> 00:02:15,405
Now, side by side.

52
00:02:15,405 --> 00:02:17,065
The angle decides the sign.

53
00:02:17,415 --> 00:02:20,964
At sixty degrees, the shadow
of A falls forward, along B.

54
00:02:20,964 --> 00:02:22,712
The dot product is positive.

55
00:02:23,112 --> 00:02:26,863
At one hundred and twenty degrees,
the shadow falls backward.

56
00:02:26,863 --> 00:02:28,691
The dot product is negative.

57
00:02:29,291 --> 00:02:30,240
Now you try.

58
00:02:30,240 --> 00:02:32,221
Theta is exactly ninety degrees.

59
00:02:32,221 --> 00:02:35,243
Is the dot product
positive, negative, or zero?

60
00:02:35,243 --> 00:02:36,423
Pause and decide.

61
00:02:39,623 --> 00:02:40,523
Zero!

62
00:02:40,139 --> 00:02:43,593
At ninety degrees, the shadow
shrinks to a single point.

63
00:02:43,593 --> 00:02:45,159
And cos ninety is zero.

64
00:02:45,809 --> 00:02:47,550
Now, a shortcut exams love.

65
00:02:47,550 --> 00:02:48,664
Follow the links.

66
00:02:49,014 --> 00:02:49,914
One.

67
00:02:49,488 --> 00:02:51,853
i hat and i hat point the same way.

68
00:02:51,853 --> 00:02:54,218
Theta is zero, so i dot i is one.

69
00:02:54,618 --> 00:02:55,518
Two.

70
00:02:55,136 --> 00:02:59,357
i hat and j hat are at ninety
degrees, so i dot j is zero.

71
00:02:59,357 --> 00:03:01,788
Same for j and k, and k and i.

72
00:03:02,188 --> 00:03:03,088
Three.

73
00:03:02,788 --> 00:03:06,202
Write A and B in i, j
and k, and multiply out.

74
00:03:06,202 --> 00:03:08,120
Every mixed pair gives zero.

75
00:03:08,520 --> 00:03:09,420
Four.

76
00:03:09,154 --> 00:03:11,293
Only matching pairs survive.

77
00:03:11,293 --> 00:03:15,912
A dot B equals A x B x,
plus A y B y, plus A z B z.

78
00:03:16,512 --> 00:03:17,412
Your turn.

79
00:03:17,360 --> 00:03:19,231
A is three i plus four j.

80
00:03:19,231 --> 00:03:21,151
B is four i minus three j.

81
00:03:21,151 --> 00:03:22,905
Are they at right angles?

82
00:03:22,905 --> 00:03:24,103
Pause and think.

83
00:03:27,303 --> 00:03:28,203
Yes!

84
00:03:27,765 --> 00:03:29,529
Twelve minus twelve is zero.

85
00:03:29,529 --> 00:03:31,945
A zero dot product means ninety degrees.

86
00:03:32,595 --> 00:03:34,285
Now, one worked example.

87
00:03:34,635 --> 00:03:37,174
A is two i, plus two j, plus k.

88
00:03:37,174 --> 00:03:39,242
B is three i, plus four k.

89
00:03:39,242 --> 00:03:42,180
Find A dot B, and the angle between them.

90
00:03:42,680 --> 00:03:44,398
Multiply matching parts.

91
00:03:44,398 --> 00:03:46,559
Six, plus zero, plus four.

92
00:03:46,559 --> 00:03:47,645
That is ten.

93
00:03:48,395 --> 00:03:49,533
Now the sizes.

94
00:03:49,533 --> 00:03:53,178
A is the root of four plus
four plus one, so three.

95
00:03:53,178 --> 00:03:56,350
B is the root of nine
plus sixteen, so five.

96
00:03:57,100 --> 00:04:00,342
Cos theta equals A dot B, over A times B.

97
00:04:00,342 --> 00:04:03,228
Ten over fifteen, which is two thirds.

98
00:04:03,978 --> 00:04:08,085
So theta is cos inverse of two
thirds, about forty eight degrees.

99
00:04:08,735 --> 00:04:10,197
Now, the exam trap.

100
00:04:10,547 --> 00:04:14,806
Many students multiply matching
parts, but keep the i, j and k.

101
00:04:14,806 --> 00:04:16,896
They write six i plus four k.

102
00:04:17,246 --> 00:04:19,466
But a dot product is a scalar.

103
00:04:19,466 --> 00:04:22,043
Add the parts into one number, ten.

104
00:04:22,043 --> 00:04:23,740
No i, no j, no k.

105
00:04:24,390 --> 00:04:25,881
Where is this asked?

106
00:04:25,881 --> 00:04:30,464
The angle between two vectors, checking
for right angles, and work as F

107
00:04:30,464 --> 00:04:31,364
dot d.

108
00:04:31,734 --> 00:04:32,977
Exam level now.

109
00:04:32,977 --> 00:04:36,082
A is four i, minus two j, plus four k.

110
00:04:36,082 --> 00:04:38,262
B is three j, plus four k.

111
00:04:38,262 --> 00:04:40,873
What is the component of A along B?

112
00:04:40,873 --> 00:04:42,168
Pause and solve.

113
00:04:47,568 --> 00:04:49,053
The answer is A.

114
00:04:49,053 --> 00:04:49,953
Two.

115
00:04:50,140 --> 00:04:53,613
A dot B is zero, minus six, plus sixteen.

116
00:04:53,613 --> 00:04:54,790
That is ten.

117
00:04:55,290 --> 00:04:59,766
The size of B is the root of
nine plus sixteen, which is five.

118
00:05:00,266 --> 00:05:03,219
The shadow of A on B is A dot B over B.

119
00:05:03,219 --> 00:05:04,836
Ten over five is two.

120
00:05:05,436 --> 00:05:06,977
Here is your recap.

121
00:05:06,977 --> 00:05:08,559
Screenshot this card.

122
00:05:11,759 --> 00:05:13,945
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

123
00:05:14,345 --> 00:05:15,245
One.

124
00:05:14,843 --> 00:05:18,271
Why is the dot product a
scalar, and not a vector?

125
00:05:19,171 --> 00:05:20,071
Two.

126
00:05:19,629 --> 00:05:22,311
When is the dot product
of two vectors zero?

127
00:05:23,211 --> 00:05:24,111
Three.

128
00:05:23,703 --> 00:05:26,898
Why does a lower handle help
Aarav pull his suitcase forward?

129
00:05:27,998 --> 00:05:32,305
Next time: carry a heavy bag across
a room, and physics says you did no

130
00:05:32,305 --> 00:05:33,205
work on it.

131
00:05:33,203 --> 00:05:34,103
Really?

132
00:05:33,808 --> 00:05:36,649
We find out in work done
by a constant force.
